Architecture Overview (Current Model)

High-Level Flow

1️⃣ X11 C/C++ backend
  •  Owns canonical window framebuffers (g_fb[]).
  •  x11_backend_fb_resize(wid, w, h) resizes backing store.
  •  x11_xproto_copy_window_bgra(host, ...):
  •  Copies host FB into scratch.
  •  Iterates mapped descendants.
  •  Calls blit_child_over_host(...).
  •  Returns composited BGRA buffer.

2️⃣ WindowTable (C++)
  •  Authoritative geometry store:
    xid, parent, x, y, w, h, mapped, presentable, dirty
  •  setGeometryRootlessHost:
  •  setGeometry(host)
  •  clampDescendantsToParent(host)
  •  Currently using Option B clamp:
  •  Clamp child x/y
  •  DO NOT clamp child w/h

3️⃣ Swift WindowRegistry
  •  Owns Cocoa NSWindow for top-level host only.
  •  Tracks:
  •  latestHostSizePxByXid
  •  lastSentHostSizePxByXid
  •  resize suppression gates
  •  windowResized:
  •  Converts Cocoa sizePixels → protocol pixels
  •  Sends sendConfigureAsync(host, wPx, hPx)
  •  applyX11Resize:
  •  Applies resize from X11 to Cocoa host
  •  schedulePresent:
  •  Host-only mode: always snapshot host
  •  C side composites children

