Most Likely Root Cause (Now That We Have Real Data)

setGeometryRootlessHost() calls:
  setGeometry(host) 
  clampDescendantsToParent(host)
But after clamp:
  •  WindowTable geometry may change for child.
  •  We resize child FB in applyRootlessResize loop.
  •  BUT child geometry can change later via:
  •  X11 ConfigureWindow on child
  •  Other protocol path
  •  That geometry update may not trigger FB resize.

Meaning:

Geometry changes must always be coupled to FB resize for windows.
Next Structural Decision

We must pick one:

Option A (Strict)

Any time setGeometry() changes a window’s w/h:
→ immediately resize its FB.

Option B (Centralized)

Only allow FB resize in:
  •  applyRootlessResize (host resize path)
  •  handleConfigureWindow (child resize path)

But ensure every geometry change funnels through one of those.

Right now, geometry and FB can diverge.

